  "evicted": {
   "text": "The old lantern had a hinge that creaked with every movement, a reminder of the past. It hung from a nail that had rotted over the years, its light casting long shadows across the room. The hinge, though worn, still held the lantern in place, a testament to the care it had received. As the wind blew, the lantern swayed, its light flickering like a flame in the dark.  \n\nThe hinge was more than just a mechanical part—it was a symbol of resilience. It had endured storms, time, and the weight of memories. In the quiet of the night, the lantern provided a soft glow, a small but steady light that guided the way.  \n\nAnd then, as the moon rose high in the sky, the lantern became more than a tool. It became a lantern of hope, a symbol of the light that could still be found even in the darkest of times. The hinge, though worn, still held the lantern in place, a silent promise that even in the most difficult moments, there was always a way forward.",
